.nh
.TH "PB-TEAM-ACTIVITY-EXPORT" "1" "Sep 2026" "Paperboat" "Paperboat CLI"

.SH NAME
pb-team-activity-export - Export the team audit log as CSV or JSON


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpb team activity export <team> [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Download every audit log event that matches the filters, newest first, as a CSV file or a JSON array, for an archive or a SIEM. The same filters as pb team activity apply. The file is written to a temporary name and renamed when complete, so a failed download never leaves a partial file. Each export is itself recorded in the audit log.

.PP
This command does not support --json output; it rejects that mode before execution. Use --help --json for structured command help.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--action\fP=""
	action, or a prefix such as team or billing

.PP
\fB--actor\fP=""
	account ID, email or API token ID

.PP
\fB--format\fP="csv"
	csv or json

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for export

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	file to write, or - for standard output

.PP
\fB--result\fP=""
	success or denied

.PP
\fB--search\fP=""
	text in the action, target name or actor email

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	start: RFC 3339 time or a duration ago such as 24h or 7d

.PP
\fB--target\fP=""
	target resource or machine ID

.PP
\fB--until\fP=""
	end: RFC 3339 time or a duration ago


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	path to the CLI config file

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	print machine-readable JSON

.PP
\fB--no-customization\fP[=false]
	ignore local shortcuts, command defaults, and TUI preferences

.PP
\fB--server\fP=""
	paperboat-server base URL override

.PP
\fB--workspace\fP=""
	resource workspace selector: personal or a team slug


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBpb-team-activity(1)\fP
